## Non-Functional Requirements
- **Non-blocking** — `PublishAsync` must not add meaningful latency to the caller's request path. Use an in-memory channel/queue plus a background dispatcher (`BackgroundService`), not a synchronous HTTP call inline.
- **Resilient** — retry with backoff and a circuit breaker (e.g. Polly) around the HEC call. A downstream Splunk failure must never throw out of `PublishAsync` or crash the host app.
- **Bounded** — cap the in-memory queue; define and document overflow behavior (e.g. drop-oldest + increment a metric) rather than growing unbounded.
- **Secure** — no secrets in source or checked-in config; support configurable field-level redaction/masking on `details` so PII can't leak into Splunk by accident.
- **Observable** — internal `ILogger` diagnostics plus counters (published / failed / dropped) so each host app's own monitoring can catch audit-pipeline problems.
- **Testable** — `IAuditPublisher` mockable; HEC client built around `IHttpClientFactory`/`HttpMessageHandler` so it's testable without a live Splunk instance.
- **Backward compatible by default** — schema changes must be additive (new optional fields) under the same major `schemaVersion`; breaking changes require a major version bump and a documented migration note. This is what keeps every isolated project's data uniform as the package evolves, not just a convention teams have to remember.

## Technical Constraints & Conventions
- Target framework: .NET 8 (LTS) minimum; multi-target `net8.0;net9.0` if practical.
- Distribution: internal NuGet package (e.g. Azure Artifacts) — each isolated solution adds it via `PackageReference`; no project-reference coupling between the independent solutions.
- Suggested package/namespace: `Infoservices.Audit.Splunk` — adjust to your actual internal naming convention.
- `System.Text.Json` with a fixed, documented naming policy (camelCase) and fixed date format — part of what keeps output identical across apps.
- Modern C# idioms: file-scoped namespaces, nullable reference types enabled, `async`/`await` throughout, XML doc comments on public members.

